A||||6||Master_Sushi||16 inch wheels||||5||
Z||000000||Master_Sushi||05-03-2001||12:31 AM||||I am looking for some new wheels/tires for my fiero. I'm really getting sick of running snow tires on stock tech wheels  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">. Now I found a place online where I can get a pair of 16X7 5-100 40S Konig wheels for a good price. I am just wondering if this is a good choice for my 88 coupe. Also, what should I do about the front and back offset difference on my 88. Would a pair of 1/2 inch spacers on the rear make it look good and not affect handling? Other then that I don't know what to do. Also tirerack says I should get 205/55-16 series tires on all four. Is this a good size? If not what should I get?<P>I appreciate any input,<BR>I just want to make sure I get the right wheels/tires.||||reg||5
Z||000001||TheFiero64||05-03-2001||04:03 PM||||I would get 205 in the front and 215 in the back. Don't let tirerack tell you any different.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||KRMFiero||05-03-2001||04:28 PM||||I have 215's on all fours...  looks alright i wish i got 225's for the back though ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Slammed Fiero||05-03-2001||04:31 PM||||for best handling get larger rear tires , skip the spacers..not a good idea for street use.<P>JM||||reg||1
Z||000004||Master_Sushi||05-03-2001||07:02 PM||||Ok, Ill go with the larger tires in the back for sure. Now im still kind of worried about the offset for my front tires. I know they stick a little bit more then the backs with my 14 inch tech wheels. Will it look ok with 16's? Also is there anything I can do about this? Thanks again.||||reg||14
Z||000005||WKDFIRO||05-03-2001||07:16 PM||||I have 225/50/16s on 16x7 all the way around my 85 GT and they look awesome. An 88 in our club has 16s all around and I believe hes running 245 Eagle GS-Cs in the back! I went for single size so I could rotate with no problems. Yes they stick out just a little in the front but not enough to take notice of and i think that it is only slightly different due to the brand of tire you choose. I have found that 225s of one brand can be bigger or smaller than others. (?)<P>There is at least one Fiero I know of with very thin spacers in the back and they actually look better. 1/2 inch is way too big I would think! Unless you have a 1/2 inch worth of bolt thread for the lugnuts!||||reg||14
Z||000006||My7Fieros||05-04-2001||01:27 AM||||16s are kind of a funky size.....youll find it alittle more difficult to find some decent tires for the right price if youve got 16s.....<BR>Most aftermarket wheels are usually 17 or 18...Id try to avoid 16s unless its one helluva deal. At least this is my expierience. M7F||||reg||1
